# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment files
#
# ONLY .env.example is committed — it is the template other people copy.
# Everything else here holds real credentials (database URL, JWT secret, Bunny
# keys, the Upstash token, the SonicPesa keys) and must never reach a remote.
# .env.local.backup is listed explicitly: it is an easy file to forget and it
# carries the same secrets as the file it backs up.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.local.*
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.development
.env.staging

# A snapshot pulled out of the hosting provider for `--env-from` — same secrets
# as .env.local, and an easy thing to create by hand and forget to delete.
.env.vercel
.env.vercel.*

# uploaded images (dev/local storage; Bunny in production)
public/uploads/

# local sandboxes and tooling
.setup-test/
.vercel/
.freebuff/
# Scratch probes: throwaway scripts that hardcode live tokens, keys and
# connection strings while debugging against production. Never shipped.
tmp-emu/
.DS_Store

# Wrangler's build output and local dev state, wherever a Worker lives — it also
# holds a local secrets file if one is ever written, which must not be committed.
.wrangler/

